  "_comment": "Which FST build the harness installs and evaluates with, per language. An evaluation PIN (tool configuration, sha256-verified where the channel allows), not a language fact: the language card says an FST EXISTS (resources.fsts[]); this file says which build the harness measures with, so a harness version pins its FST version. Shipped inside the wheel so it works from a pip install and on an air-gapped node. Recovered 2026-10-03 from the pre-atlas cards (git 1b8cccc5f^), where these blocks lived as resources.fsts[0].install until the 2026-08-12 cutover dropped them and silently turned the FST metrics off. Override with MT_EVAL_FST_PINS=<path to a file of this shape>. Re-pinning crk requires a regression run (see the note on its entry).",
