      "note": "Pinned to the GiellaLT NIGHTLY build of lang-crk @ bec054ef (2026-09-29), not to a GitHub release: upstream's newest release tag (fst-v2021.7.8) is five years stale and uses 'y' where current lang-crk uses 'ý', so generation silently failed for 17.6% of lemmas. Re-pinned 2026-10-03 from e1f96fea (2026-06-03), which the nightly pool had pruned, after a regression run: the six analyzer/generator files are byte-identical to e1f96fea's, analyser-gt-desc differs only by two unused tags (+Use/TTS, +Use/-TTS), and 8,039 surfaces from lang-crk's own test yamls analyse identically on both builds (0 regressions). Upstream gaps unchanged on both: namôya, mwêstas, nisis, okîsikâw, êwako, kotak. Newer is not automatically better: re-pin only after the same check."
